%description:

TcpCubic.beta:invalid -- a factor of 1 stops the run with an error.

The claim: the code accepts a factor above 0 and below 1.

The classes: rfc9438 (0.7, the default, the value of RFC 9438), other (another value between 0
and 1), invalid (0 and less, 1 and more). The code: TcpCubic::calculateSsthresh() returns
max(floor(segCwnd * beta), 2) segments; TcpCubic::initializeAlgorithm() checks the value.

Host under test: host1, with TcpCubic, whose algorithm reads the parameter at the open.
Observation: the error, and the exit code of the run.

%# parameter: TcpCubic.beta
%# class: invalid
%# value: 1.0
%# key: *.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.beta
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpCubicBetaInvalid compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.beta = 1.0    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "TcpCubic"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
beta must be more than 0 and less than 1, but it is 1
